   "text": "**Step 26 plan: combine everything measured so far into one classifier.** Step 25 decoded cleanly. Up-end in the four top-left cells, by digit:\n\n| Digit | Any up-end here |\n|---|---|\n| 0 | 3% |\n| 1 | 10% |\n| 2 | 1% |\n| 3 | 1% |\n| 4 | 72% |\n| 5 | 7% |\n| 6 | 1% |\n| 7 | 6% |\n| 8 | 3% |\n| 9 | 1% |\n\nThat is the 4's left arm, and it is almost exclusive to 4. The extra, \"/\" at (row 3, col 1), ranges from 55% to 92% across digits (highest for 2 and 8), so it is only mildly informative.\n\nThis step's classifier has two parts:\n\n1. **Presence/absence vote**, as in step 20 at scale 0.25, with the two newly measured \"/\" cells added at full weight.\n2. **Endpoint vote** (new). For each endpoint group (up-left, up-right, left, right, down) I have, per digit, the share of images with no end and the share whose strongest end is in each cell. The weight on each endpoint cell is the log-ratio of \"end here\" to \"no end\", and the bias takes the log of \"no end\". For the three groups probed nine ways, the catch-all outcome becomes one shared weight on the pooled cells. This part is scaled by 0.6, and the cell weights by a further 0.7 because detector outputs often exceed 1.\n\nThe expected effect is on 3\u21948, 5\u21948, 2\u21948, 9\u21943, 9\u21947, 0\u21942 and 4\u21949, where the endpoint rates differ by large factors.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport math\n\n\ndef build_weights():\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # conv1: 4 oriented line detectors x 2 thresholds  (unchanged)\n    #   channel k   (k=0..3): orientation k, bias -t0\n    #   channel k+4         : same filter,  bias -t1\n    #   orientation 0: horizontal stroke, 1: \"/\" , 2: vertical, 3: \"\\\"\n    #   pooled(k) - pooled(k+4) = clip(resp - t0, 0, t1 - t0)  -> saturated map M_k\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    prof = np.array([-0.75, 0.25, 1.0, 0.25, -0.75])   # across-stroke profile (zero sum)\n    Hf = np.tile(prof[:, None], (1, 5))                # horizontal stroke detector\n    Vf = Hf.T.copy()                                   # vertical stroke detector\n    dv = [1.0, 0.4, -0.45, -0.9, -0.95]                # diagonal profile by |offset| (zero sum)\n    D1 = np.zeros((5, 5))\n    D2 = np.zeros((5, 5))\n    for r in range(5):\n        for c in range(5):\n            D1[r, c] = dv[abs((r - 2) + (c - 2))]      # \"/\" : ridge on r + c = 4\n            D2[r, c] = dv[abs((r - 2) - (c - 2))]      # \"\\\" : ridge on r = c\n    filts = [Hf, D1, Vf, D2]\n    t0, t1 = 0.45, 0.75\n    w1 = np.zeros((8, 1, 5, 5))\n    b1 = np.zeros(8)\n    for k in range(4):\n        w1[k, 0] = filts[k] / 5.0\n        b1[k] = -t0\n        w1[k + 4, 0] = filts[k] / 5.0\n        b1[k + 4] = -t1\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    # conv2:\n    #   channels 0..3  : C_k  = stroke amount of orientation k (unused by the fc layer now)\n    #   channels 4..7  : E_k  = ReLU(1 - amount/tau)   (\"stroke k missing here\"; 0 = present)\n    #   channels 8..11 : C'_k = ReLU(amount - tau_l)   (unused by the fc layer now)\n    #   channels 12..15: stroke-end detectors (up, down, left, right)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n    k1 = np.array([0.5, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 0.5])\n    K2 = np.outer(k1, k1)\n    tau = 1.6\n    tau_l = 1.5\n    w2 = np.zeros((16, 8, 5, 5))\n    b2 = np.zeros(16)\n    for k in range(4):\n        w2[k, k] = K2 / (t1 - t0)\n        w2[k, k + 4] = -K2 / (t1 - t0)\n        w2[4 + k, k] = -K2 / ((t1 - t0) * tau)\n        w2[4 + k, k + 4] = K2 / ((t1 - t0) * tau)\n        b2[4 + k] = 1.0\n        w2[8 + k, k] = K2 / (t1 - t0)\n        w2[8 + k, k + 4] = -K2 / (t1 - t0)\n        b2[8 + k] = -tau_l\n\n    def setM(ch, k, r, c, w):\n        # add weight w on the saturated orientation map M_k at kernel position (r, c)\n        w2[ch, k, r, c] += w / (t1 - t0)\n        w2[ch, k + 4, r, c] -= w / (t1 - t0)\n\n    HH, DS, VV, DB = 0, 1, 2, 3     # orientation indices: horizontal, \"/\", vertical, \"\\\"\n    INH = 4.0                       # strength of the \"nothing beyond the tip\" inhibition\n\n    # up-end (channel 12): tip at kernel (1,2), stroke continues to (2,2), nothing in row 0\n    for (r, wt) in [(1, 0.75), (2, 0.25)]:\n        setM(12, VV, r, 2, wt)\n        setM(12, DS, r, 2, 0.5 * wt)\n        setM(12, DB, r, 2, 0.5 * wt)\n    for c in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(12, k, 0, c, -INH)         # any ink above the tip\n        setM(12, HH, 1, c, -INH)            # a horizontal stroke capping the tip\n\n    TIPD = 0.6      # weight of a diagonal stroke at the tip (down/left/right detectors)\n\n    # down-end (channel 13): tip at kernel (3,2), stroke continues to (2,2), nothing in row 4\n    setM(13, VV, 3, 2, 0.75)\n    setM(13, DS, 3, 2, TIPD)\n    setM(13, DB, 3, 2, TIPD)\n    setM(13, VV, 2, 2, 0.25)\n    setM(13, DS, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    setM(13, DB, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    for c in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(13, k, 4, c, -INH)\n        setM(13, HH, 3, c, -INH)\n\n    # left-end (channel 14): tip at kernel (2,1), stroke continues to (2,2), nothing in column 0\n    setM(14, HH, 2, 1, 0.75)\n    setM(14, DS, 2, 1, TIPD)\n    setM(14, DB, 2, 1, TIPD)\n    setM(14, HH, 2, 2, 0.25)\n    setM(14, DS, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    setM(14, DB, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    for r in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(14, k, r, 0, -INH)\n        setM(14, VV, r, 1, -INH)\n\n    # right-end (channel 15): tip at kernel (2,3), stroke continues to (2,2), nothing in column 4\n    setM(15, HH, 2, 3, 0.75)\n    setM(15, DS, 2, 3, TIPD)\n    setM(15, DB, 2, 3, TIPD)\n    setM(15, HH, 2, 2, 0.25)\n    setM(15, DS, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    setM(15, DB, 2, 2, 0.125)\n    for r in (1, 2, 3):\n        for k in range(4):\n            setM(15, k, r, 4, -INH)\n        setM(15, VV, r, 3, -INH)\n\n    # ----------------------